’s scores align with results seen across the country and with what was seen on this year’s 2022 School Report Card.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"96ca9a9c3b90d66c\">>>", "published": "October 24, 2022", "siteName": "www.kentuckyteacher.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"be95d8f94be64e3d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: Mathematics Highlights 2022\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"be95d8f94be64e3d\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"dfb9c6d837041918\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nDownload a summary of the 2022 mathematics results. Scroll to read details for each grade or select items in the table of contents. ... Results for states/jurisdictions reflect the performance of students in public schools only and are reported along with the results for public school students in the nation. Figure Change in average scores between 2019 and 2022 for fourth-grade public school students in NAEP mathematics, by state/jurisdiction\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"dfb9c6d837041918\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"58657d0830ce69f2\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNOVEMBER 2022\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"58657d0830ce69f2\">>>", "url": "https://csgsouth.org/wp-content/uploads/QofM-November.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b24b50b3ecfbbe73\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nOn October 24, 2022, the United States Department of Education’s National Center for Education Statistics (NCES) released the results of the National Assessment of Education Progress (NAEP) – commonly referred to as “The Nation’s · Report Card.” Due to the pandemic’s impact, the national average scores in mathematics for fourth- and eighth-graders\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b24b50b3ecfbbe73\">>>", "siteName": "csgsouth.org"}]}, "isError": false, "timesta