{"type": "message", "id": "c5e4c19b", "parentId": "c430dc0e", "timestamp": "2026-04-08T11:25:29.128Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_c4b00cb0fcae4edf9c2a1415", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"Arizona NAEP 8th grade math 2022 score\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 993,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"502778400c158531\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT ARIZONA  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"502778400c158531\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011AZ8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"71ef57ec3e562c90\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAVERAGE SCORES FOR STATE/JURISDICTION AND THE NATION (PUBLIC) ... White students. This performance gap was not significantly different from that in 2000 ... NOTE: <strong>The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from 0 to 500</strong>. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"71ef57ec3e562c90\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"561665211ae683c9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: Mathematics Highlights 2022\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"561665211ae683c9\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"34c5137d4840d406\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDownload a summary of the 2022 mathematics results. Scroll to read details for each grade or select items in the table of contents. ... Results for states/jurisdictions reflect the performance of students in public schools only and are reported along with the results for public school students in the nation. Figure Change in average scores between 2019 and 2022 for fourth-grade public school students in NAEP mathematics, by state/jurisdiction\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"34c5137d4840d406\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7cd8894a851ed432\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7cd8894a851ed432\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fc286054f77b15fc\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTo compare average mathematics scores between states/jurisdictions and the nation (public), use the NAEP State Profiles Tool. ... In the 43 states/jurisdictions where scores were lower in 2022 than 2019, the size of the score differences ranged from 2 to 14 points. The average score decline for public schools in the nation decreased by 5 points. To view score changes for fourth-grade ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fc286054f77b15fc\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d63ac1ee2e46dd79\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 National Assessment of Educational Progress Grade 8 Mathematics Results\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d63ac1ee2e46dd79\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.fldoe.org/core/fileparse.php/7667/urlt/2022NAEPGrade8Math.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bfb7d1efcda16852\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOTE: The NAEP Mathematics scale ranges from <strong>0 to 500</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bfb7d1efcda16852\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.fldoe.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8b9451797c791d67\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe New NAEP Scores Highlight a Standards Gap in Many States - FutureEd\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8b9451797c791d67\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.future-ed.org/the-new-naep-scores-highlight-a-standards-gap-in-many-states/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"11737851cc9fdb09\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nForty-seven states improved NAEP math proficiency rates between 2022 and 2024 in fourth grade and 36 states did so in eighth grade. But proficiency rates remain below 2019 levels in 34 states in fourth-grade and in all but one state in eighth-grade. Similarly, math proficiency rates rose on nearly every state’s standardized tests during the same period. While state math scores declined dramatically between 2019 and 2022, particularly in eighth grade, only in Arizona, Arkansas, Florida, Idaho, and Vermont in fourth grade and Arkansas, Michigan, and Missouri in eighth grade did state test scores decline between 2022 and 2024.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"11737851cc9fdb09\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 10, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.future-ed.org\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "Arizona NAEP 8th grade math 2022 score", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 993, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"502778400c158531\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT ARIZONA  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"502778400c158531\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011AZ8.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"71ef57